{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 30, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Hark good traveler of this fair and distant land\nUpon thy journey to Japan’s fair isle\nA quill I shall wield with ink most grand\nTo spin thee an itinerary most hale\n\n**Upon the First Morn of Thy Voyage**\nAwake with the sun in Tokyo’s bright glow\nTo Nihonbashi bridge do thou hasten forth\nWhere neon and tradition do hand in hand bestow\nThe Sumida River’s gentle flow to behold and adore\n\nAt Asakusa’s temple where lanterns gleam\nKannon’s gaze shall bless thee with quiet dream\nA ryokan’s embrace where tatami does lie\nAnd onsen’s steam shall cleanse both flesh and eye\n\n**The Second Dawn Shall See Thee Roam**\nTo Akihabara’s heart where tech doth sing\nAnime’s bright world and gadgets that do cling\nYet stray thou must to Ueno’s park so fair\nWhere cherry blossoms in spring’s sweet air do spare\n\nAt a quaint izakaya let thy hunger be fed\nWith yakitori and sake where merry souls are wed\nThen to Shibuya’s scramble where crowds do mass\nYet in its quiet corners peace doth pass\n\n**On the Third Day Let Thy Spirit Soar**\nTo Nikko’s shrine where gods in wood do dwell\nKegon Falls shall whisper tales both old and fell\nThe Toshogu Shrine with gold that doth gleam\nA pilgrim’s path where ancient souls do seem\n\nAt Obaku Temple’s gate let thy thoughts align\nWith Zen’s calm where earth and heaven intertwine\nThen to the mountains where air is crisp and clean\nA hike through Kegon’s woods where nature’s rhythm convenes\n\n**The Fourth Shall Bear Thee to Kyoto’s Grace**\nTo Fushimi Inari where torii’s sea does rise\nA hike ‘neath their crimson banners ‘neath open skies\nAt Kinkaku-ji where gold leaf shines\nA pavilion of dreams in twilight’s vines\n\nThe Arashiyama Bamboo where whispers play\nA forest of stalks that sway and sway\nAt Gion’s lantern-lit streets where geisha tread\nA glimpse of old Japan where time is led\n\n**Upon the Fifth Shall Come Osaka’s Might**\nTo Dotonbori’s neon and laughter so loud\nTakoyaki’s crisp bite and ramen bowl’s proud\nThe Osaka Castle where samurai once stood\nNow stands as a symbol of days that are wowed\n\nAt Universal Studios let thy heart take flight\nWhere heroes and villains in celestial light\nDo battle and dance in worlds both bright and wide\nA respite from travel where joy doth abide\n\n**The Sixth Shall Send Thee to Hiroshima’s Light**\nWhere peace doth dwell ‘neath skies that shine so bright\nThe Atom Bomb Dome where history’s weight does press\nYet new life blooms in Miyajima’s bay\nWhere Itsukushima’s shrine doth sway\n\nA moment of silence where hope does rise\nIn a land that once knew sorrow and surprise\nNow stands renewed with courage and grace\nA beacon of peace in this modern space\n\n**On the Seventh Day Let Thy Journey Wind Down**\nTo Miyajima’s deer where bells do chime\nAnd momiji manju’s sweet crumbs dost climb\nA final stroll ‘neath Mount Misen’s crown\nWhere fireworks at night shall weave a dazzling gown\n\n**And Lo The Eighth Shall See Thee Depart**\nWith memories bright and heart filled with cheer\nFrom Tokyo’s bustle to Kyoto’s serene sphere\nJapan hath kissed thee with stories untold\nA land where old and new in perfect accord hold\n\nFarewell dear traveler with spirit so keen\nMay thy path be blessed ‘neath the rising sun’s sheen\nAnd shouldst thou ever return to this fair isle\nJapan’s embrace shall welcome thee with gentle smile.", "logprobs": [{"token": "H", "logprob": -0.16029712557792664}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.0027155925054103136}, {"token": " good", "logprob": -1.7217481136322021}, {"token": " travel", "logprob": -0.5338188409805298}, {"token": "er", "logprob": -0.0007026110542938113}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -2.1656064987182617}, {"token": " this", "logprob": -3.7241735458374023}, {"token": " fair", "logprob": -0.982107400894165}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.5983999967575073}, {"token": " distant", "logpro